# Stint local environment example.
# Copy to `.env.local` for Next.js development (never commit real secrets):
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# After `pnpm supabase:start`, copy values from `pnpm supabase:status`.
# Prefer the CLI "Publishable" key. Older CLI output may label it "anon key";
# paste that browser-safe value into NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY.

# --- Browser-safe (exposed to the client via NEXT_PUBLIC_*) ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=replace-with-local-publishable-or-anon-key

# Optional canonical origin for Auth email redirects (production: https://klinnova.com).
# Local default falls back to http://localhost:3000 when unset.
# Preview falls back to the Vercel deployment URL when unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional Sentry DSN (M5.1 Unit G). Sentry.init() no-ops without a DSN, so
# this is safe to leave unset locally. Production Sentry remains OFF/unwired
# by Founder decision for Cohort A. Never set this to a value containing a
# secret; DSNs are public identifiers by design, but SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN
# (source-map upload, build-time only) is a genuine secret and must never
# appear here or anywhere with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# --- Server-only ---
# No privileged server secrets are required for Auth foundation (PR 1.2).
# Browser and ordinary SSR sessions use the publishable key + user cookies only.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY / secret keys remain deferred.
# Do not expose privileged keys with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.

# Business transactional-email foundation (N1, src/lib/mail/**). Conceptually
# distinct from Supabase Auth email above — no application business email is
# triggered yet (N2/N3 remain separately authorized future units). Required
# only if you are exercising src/lib/mail/** locally; leave unset otherwise.
# MAIL_TRANSPORT=resend
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN / SENTRY_ORG / SENTRY_PROJECT are build-time-only
# source-map-upload inputs (M5.1 Unit G2, not yet authorized) — never set
# locally, never with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
